Chapter: BvtResidentFall
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeGameRules
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 UOAIX-143 (trial 42626): a resident killed by a monster kept its vendor owner row until its own step, and the save check
 named "mobile missing". A founded composite on open land; resident 0 dies at the blow (cg-residents-fall).
  brf-fill : WalkMap, Integer -> Integer
  brf-fill (map) (i) = if i == map.width * map.height then 0
    else let mark = __heap-save
    in let result = walk-set-land map (map.x + int-mod i map.width) (map.y + i / map.width) 0 0
    in let restored = __heap-restore mark in brf-fill map (i + 1)
  brf-founded : Integer -> Result CompositeGame Text
  brf-founded (unused) = when walk-map-new 1408 1520 96 240
    is Err (e) -> Err e
    is Ok (britain) -> let filled = brf-fill britain 0
      in when cg-britain britain
        is Err (e) -> Err e
        is Ok (owner) -> when cg-install owner (CompositeSetup { vendor-z = 0, shrine-z = 0, home-z = 0, decoration = None })
          is Err (e) -> Err e
          is Ok (_) -> Ok owner
 Answers a bit per check: 1 resident 0 holds an owner row before, 2 an unknown serial settles nobody and changes no row,
 4 the resident settles once, 8 its row is gone and every other row stays; 15 is all.
  brf-checks : Integer -> Integer
  brf-checks (unused) = when brf-founded 0
    is Err (_) -> 0 - 1
    is Ok (owner) -> when owner.town
      is None -> 0 - 2
      is Just (t) -> if t.count < 1 then 0 - 3
        else let r = list-at t.residents 0
        in let serial = (tf-person t.people r.person).world-serial
        in let v = owner.vendor
        in let rows = v.owner-count
        in let held = gv-owner v serial 0 >= 0
        in let stranger = cg-residents-fall t 999999999 0
        in let same = v.owner-count == rows
        in let fell = cg-residents-fall t serial 0
        in (if held then 1 else 0) + (if stranger == 0 & same then 2 else 0) + (if fell == 1 then 4 else 0)
          + (if gv-owner v serial 0 < 0 & v.owner-count == rows - 1 then 8 else 0)
  bvt-resident-fall : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-resident-fall (unused) = act
    n <- brf-checks 0
    a <- bvt-check ("a resident killed at the blow loses its owner row, and no other row moves (cg-residents-fall, code " & show n & ")") (n == 15)
    a
  end
